A||||3||GodSend||Exaust tip adjustment||||5||
Z||000000||GodSend||04-06-2001||11:45 AM||||  My pass. side factory tips are hanging a little low.  I crawled under the car a bit to take a look and I can see where the tips meet the exaust pipe (right after the bend, and just before the hangr).<P>  It looks like they just fit on (could not see a bracket or anything).  Its mightly rusty down there, so obviously adjustment by hand is out of the question.<P>  I thought about a slab of wood and a few taps with a hammer, but there has to be a better (easier) way, any suggestions?<P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.hypernetcommunications.com/revn.gif"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Bruce||04-06-2001||03:10 PM||||I soaked mine with penetrating oil, let it set for a while, and the adjustment went prety easy.<BR>bb||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroJoe||04-06-2001||10:51 PM||||If you havent tried the penetrating oil method yet, the way I always get muffler parts off is with my acetlyene torch.  But then, I am usually cutting.  If you kept it cool enough, Im sure you could heat it just enough to be able to break it loose with a few whacks of the hammer (and the block of wood) and be all set.<P>------------------<BR>AIM: Snowboarder0311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto in progress<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||sjp777||04-06-2001||11:01 PM||||It's probably not that the tips have turned down in the pipe. It's more likely the hanger on that side is sagging. Once the tip piece is in the exhaust pipe, it rusts in place and is not likely to move, up or down.<BR>Try a generic hanger from an auto parts store and adjust it short enough to pull the tips up where you want them||||reg||1
